{"title":"Descartes Rule of Signs","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Descartes' rule of signs is a method used to determine the number of positive and negative roots of a polynomial. The rule gives an upper bound on the number of positive or negative roots, but does not specify the exact amount. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Positive_roots\">Positive roots</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes_Rule_of_Signs&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Positive roots\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If the terms of a polynomial with real coefficients are ordered by descending variable exponent, then the number of positive roots of the polynomial is equal to the number of sign differences between consecutive nonzero coefficients or is less than that by an even number. Multiple roots are counted separately.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Negative_roots\">Negative roots</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes_Rule_of_Signs&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Negative roots\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The bound for negative roots is a corollary of the positive root bound. The number of negative roots is the number of sign changes after multiplying the coefficients of odd-power terms by −1, or fewer than that by a positive even number.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes_Rule_of_Signs&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomials\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Polynomials\">Polynomials</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem\" title=\"Factor Theorem\">Factor Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_Root_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rational Root Theorem\">Rational Root Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra/Intermediate\" title=\"Algebra/Intermediate\">Algebra/Intermediate</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes_Rule_of_Signs&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017155048\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 15/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 310/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.886      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.886      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12537:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017155048 and revision id 283747. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}